  "question": "A screw gauge gives the following readings when used to measure the diameter of a wire\n\nMain scale reading : $0$ mm\n\nCircular scale reading : $52$ divisions\n\nGiven that $1$ mm on main scale corresponds to $100$ divisions on the circular scale. The diameter of the wire from the above data is :",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$0.052$ cm",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$0.52$ cm",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$0.026$ cm",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$0.26$ cm",
      "image": ""
    }
  ],
  "answer": "A",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "Least count $= \\dfrac{1\\ \\text{mm}}{100} = 0.01$ mm.\n\n$$d = 0 + 52 \\times 0.01 = 0.52\\ \\text{mm} = 0.052\\ \\text{cm}$$",
